# Code owners: the security-critical surface of the app.
#
# The scope is narrow on purpose: only paths where a silent change can weaken
# authentication, authorization, session handling, secrets or the transport
# security headers. GitHub asks the code owner to review a pull request that
# touches one of them. This file enforces nothing by itself: the review is
# required only when the repository's ruleset turns on code owner review.

# --- Authentication, sessions, tokens, TOTP, password + reset flows
/src/backend/app/auth/                @AaronKokal
/src/backend/app/routers/auth.py      @AaronKokal
/src/backend/app/routers/me.py        @AaronKokal

# --- Authorization surface: org bootstrap + membership are privilege boundaries
/src/backend/app/routers/organizations.py  @AaronKokal

# --- Secrets, JWT config, auth feature flags (e.g. enforce_org_admin_totp)
/src/backend/app/config.py            @AaronKokal

# --- App wiring: CSP + security headers, exception handlers, middleware stack
/src/backend/app/main.py              @AaronKokal
/src/backend/app/exceptions.py        @AaronKokal
/src/backend/app/middleware/          @AaronKokal

# --- Frontend security surface: security headers + the auth-routing interceptor
/src/frontend/nginx.conf              @AaronKokal
/src/frontend/src/api/client.ts       @AaronKokal

# --- Supply chain: a workflow change decides what CI runs and with which permissions
